content:
Enterprise console frontend is built and typed against /enterprise/*. Here are the exact JSON shapes I coded to — authoritative source is frontend/enterprise/src/types/{events,campaign,api}.ts, and every shape has a working fixture in src/services/mockData.ts you can copy for seeds. If any of these disagree with what you're emitting, tell me and I'll adapt (cheap on my side) — I'd rather converge now than at demo time.

WS /enterprise/ws/events — ns_event
{id:int, ts:iso8601, layer:"sensing"|"case"|"discovery"|"compiler"|"registry"|"propagation"|"exposure", event_type:str, severity:"info"|"warning"|"critical", payload:{...}, run_id:str|null}
I accept either a single object or a JSON array per frame. Anything failing the guard is silently dropped, so `id` must be a number and `layer` must be one of the seven.

payload keys I read (everything else is displayed generically, so nothing breaks if you add fields):
- call_received: {channel, case_number}
- case_ingested: {case_number, case_id}
- entity_linked: {case_number, entity, entity_type}
- case_linked: {pair:[case_id,case_id], score}
- cluster_formed: {size}
- campaign_proposed: {campaign_id, code, case_count}   ← severity should be "critical"
- campaign_approved: {campaign_id, approved_by} / campaign_rejected: {reason}
- artifact_compiled: {name, tier, version, source_campaigns?}
- artifact_published: {name, from_version, version}
- artifact_rolled_back: {name, version}
- propagated: {agent}  ← agent MUST be one of phone_agent | fraud_ops | phishing_agent | txn_monitor for the worker node to light up
- mcp_call: {caller, tool, role, latency_ms}
- eval_completed: {label, detected, total}
- unrecognised_pattern: {observations}

REST
GET /overview → {counters:{cases,open_cases,unrecognised,campaigns,core_version,exposure_rm}, metrics:[{label,before_value,after_value,unit,lower_is_better}], mode:"LIVE"|"REPLAY"}
GET /cases → {cases:[CaseSummary], total}
GET /cases/{id} → CaseSummary + {transcript:[{t:"mm:ss",speaker:"CALLER|USER|AI|SYSTEM",text,score:int|null,novel_phrases:[str]}], mo:{impersonates,pretext,phases:[str],money_ask_at,channel,language}, narrative, entities:[{id,entity_type,value_raw,value_norm,case_count}], trace:[{name,duration_ms,detail}]}
  → IMPORTANT: novel_phrases must be attached to the specific transcript line where the phrase was said (verbatim substring of that line's text) — I highlight in place and the match is case-insensitive substring. A flat top-level list of novel phrases won't render.
GET /graph → {nodes:[{id,kind:"case"|"entity"|"campaign",label,entity_type?,campaign_id?,risk_score?,case_count?}], links:[{source,target,kind:"case-entity"|"case-case"|"campaign-case",weight:0..1,reason:str,signals?,case_refs?}], hulls:[{campaign_id,code,name,node_ids:[str],colour?}]}
  → `reason` is required and non-empty on every link; it's the hover text ("shared ACCOUNT 1592… · w 0.95 · cases #7,#19").
GET /campaigns → {campaigns:[CampaignSummary]}
GET /campaigns/{id} → summary + {evidence:[{label,value,passed:bool}], hypothesis:{name,mo_summary,novel_indicators:[str]}, proposed_artifacts:[{name,tier:"core"|"pack",target_agent,version,note?,source_campaigns?}], case_ids:[str]}
  → evidence is the COMPUTED column, hypothesis is the LLM column. Please keep them as two separate top-level keys; the visual separation is the whole point of that screen.
POST /campaigns/{id}/approve → {ok:true}; POST .../reject body {reason} → {ok:true}; PATCH /campaigns/{id} body {name?,mo_summary?} → CampaignDetail
GET /artifacts?tier= → {artifacts:[{name,tier,target_agent,latest_version,versions:[ArtifactVersion desc by version]}]}, ArtifactVersion = {id,name,tier,artifact_type,target_agent,version,status:"DRAFT"|"PUBLISHED"|"ROLLED_BACK",created_at,created_by,approved_by,source_campaigns:[str],campaign_id,effectiveness:{eval_run_id,detected,total,fp,fp_total,measured_at}|null}
GET /artifacts/{name}/{version|latest} → ArtifactVersion + {content:str, previous_content:str|null, previous_version:int|null}
  → I render the red/green diff purely from content vs previous_content, so please return previous_content server-side rather than making me fetch v(n-1).
POST /artifacts/{name}/rollback body {version} → {ok:true}
POST /eval/run → {run_id,label,status}; GET /eval/latest → {before:EvalRunSummary|null, after:EvalRunSummary|null}, EvalRunSummary = {run_id,label,started_at,detected,total,false_positives,fp_total,mean_latency_ms,artifact_ver:{name:version}}
GET /mcp/log → {entries:[{id,ts,caller,role,tool,params,latency_ms,citations:[str],redacted_fields:[str]}]} (newest first)
POST /demo/scenario body {mode:"live"|"replay",speed} → {run_id,mode,speed}; POST /demo/reset → {ok:true}

THREE AMBIGUITIES I had to make a call on — please confirm or correct:
1. REPLAY source. §15 says REPLAY streams a recorded ns_events sequence. I implemented it client-side (ReplayEventSource replays at the recorded relative gaps) and I look for the recording at GET /enterprise/demo/replay first, then /replay_sequence.json, then a bundled fixture. That endpoint is NOT in the §13 table. Either (a) add GET /enterprise/demo/replay returning {events:[ns_event]} or a bare array, or (b) tell me POST /demo/scenario {mode:"replay"} makes the backend push the recording over the same WS — in which case I'll drop the client-side replay and just flip the badge. (a) is my preference: it survives a dead backend on stage.
2. Case list filters. I send /cases?tier=&campaign_id=&state=&since=&limit= as optional query params. Confirm the param names.
3. Discovery trigger. I call POST /enterprise/discovery/run (not in the §13 table) from the api client but nothing in the UI depends on it yet — drop it if you're not exposing it.

Also: I do NOT poll anything. Screens re-fetch only when a relevant ns_event arrives (e.g. the registry refetches on layer compiler|registry, the MCP log on mcp_call, eval on eval_completed). So if an action changes state, please emit the corresponding ns_event or the UI won't notice.
